===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*skend-}}
The {{lg|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|skaine}}, {{m|enm|skayne|t=quantity of string, thread, etc., wound on a reel; the string, thread, etc., so wound}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=skaine|pos=n|id=MED40605}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|escaigne}} (modern {{cog|fr|écagne}}, {{m|fr|écaigne}} {{qualifier|Picardy}}); further etymology uncertain,<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=1196329536|date=September 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> probably from {{der|en|cel-pro|-}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skend-|t=to split off}}.

The {{lg|verb}} is derived from noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=2815021853|date=September 2025}}</ref>

